{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kyuyw9Wni359WGLYKsVU9Z","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { actions, isInputError } from 'astro:actions';\n     2→import { useState } from 'react';\n     3→import {createLoggerFromFlags} from \"../../../../../src/cli/flags.ts\";\n     4→\n     5→export function PostComment({\n     6→\tpostId,\n     7→\tserverBodyError,\n     8→}: {\n     9→\tpostId: string;\n    10→\tserverBodyError?: string;\n    11→}) {\n    12→\tconst [comments, setComments] = useState<{ author: string; body: string }[]>([]);\n    13→\tconst [bodyError, setBodyError] = useState<string | undefined>(serverBodyError);\n    14→\tconst [unexpectedError, setUnexpectedError] = useState<string | undefined>(undefined);\n    15→\n    16→\treturn (\n    17→\t\t<>\n    18→\t\t\t<form\n    19→\t\t\t\tmethod=\"POST\"\n    20→\t\t\t\tdata-testid=\"client\"\n    21→\t\t\t\taction={actions.blog.comment.toString()}\n    22→\t\t\t\tonSubmit={async (e) => {\n    23→\t\t\t\t\te.preventDefault();\n    24→\t\t\t\t\tconst form = e.target as HTMLFormElement;\n    25→\t\t\t\t\tconst formData = new FormData(form);\n    26→\t\t\t\t\tconst { data, error } = await actions.blog.comment(formData);\n    27→\t\t\t\t\tif (isInputError(error)) {\n    28→\t\t\t\t\t\treturn setBodyError(error.fields.body?.join(' '));\n    29→\t\t\t\t\t} else if (error) {\n    30→\t\t\t\t\t\treturn setUnexpectedError(`${error.code}: ${error.message}`);\n    31→\t\t\t\t\t}\n    32→\t\t\t\t\tsetBodyError(undefined);\n    33→\t\t\t\t\tsetComments((c) => [data, ...c]);\n    34→\t\t\t\t\tform.reset();\n    35→\t\t\t\t}}\n    36→\t\t\t>\n    37→\t\t\t\t{unexpectedError && (\n    38→\t\t\t\t\t<p data-error=\"unexpected\" style={{ color: 'red' }}>\n    39→\t\t\t\t\t\t{unexpectedError}\n    40→\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n    41→\t\t\t\t)}\n    42→\t\t\t\t<input type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value={postId} />\n    43→\t\t\t\t<label htmlFor=\"author\">Author</label>\n    44→\t\t\t\t<input id=\"author\" type=\"text\" name=\"author\" placeholder=\"Your name\" />\n    45→\t\t\t\t<textarea rows={10} name=\"body\"></textarea>\n    46→\t\t\t\t{bodyError && (\n    47→\t\t\t\t\t<p data-error=\"body\" style={{ color: 'red' }}>\n    48→\t\t\t\t\t\t{bodyError}\n    49→\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n    50→\t\t\t\t)}\n    51→\t\t\t\t<button type=\"submit\">Post</button>\n    52→\t\t\t</form>\n    53→\t\t\t<div data-testid=\"client-comments\">\n    54→\t\t\t\t{comments.map((c) => (\n    55→\t\t\t\t\t<article\n    56→\t\t\t\t\t\tkey={c.body}\n    57→\t\t\t\t\t\tstyle={{\n    58→\t\t\t\t\t\t\tborder: '2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent), transparent 80%)',\n    59→\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpadding: '0.3rem 1rem',\n    60→\t\t\t\t\t\t\tborderRadius: '0.3rem',\n    61→\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmarginBlock: '0.3rem',\n    62→\t\t\t\t\t\t}}\n    63→\t\t\t\t\t>\n    64→\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>{c.body}</p>\n    65→\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>{c.author}</p>\n    66→\t\t\t\t\t</article>\n    67→\t\t\t\t))}\n    68→\t\t\t</div>\n    69→\t\t</>\n    70→\t);\n    71→}\n    72→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01REm1BFVwZQZT3gEYb6usDZ","session_id":"ca373184-55de-43ea-b9dc-c45b48d70f8a","uuid":"4ff78e1a-0d5d-48e7-b0c0-cda89cc6bc81"}
