{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZCwT8t1gHVqEkaCxAfv3f","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Generated by simple:form\n     2→\n     3→import { navigate } from 'astro:transitions/client';\n     4→import {\n     5→\ttype FieldErrors,\n     6→\ttype FormState,\n     7→\ttype FormValidator,\n     8→\tformNameInputProps,\n     9→\tgetInitialFormState,\n    10→\ttoSetValidationErrors,\n    11→\ttoTrackAstroSubmitStatus,\n    12→\ttoValidateField,\n    13→\tvalidateForm,\n    14→} from 'simple:form';\n    15→import { type ComponentProps, createContext, useContext, useState } from 'react';\n    16→\n    17→export function useCreateFormContext(validator: FormValidator, fieldErrors?: FieldErrors) {\n    18→\tconst initial = getInitialFormState({ validator, fieldErrors });\n    19→\tconst [formState, setFormState] = useState<FormState>(initial);\n    20→\treturn {\n    21→\t\tvalue: formState,\n    22→\t\tset: setFormState,\n    23→\t\tsetValidationErrors: toSetValidationErrors(setFormState),\n    24→\t\tvalidateField: toValidateField(setFormState),\n    25→\t\ttrackAstroSubmitStatus: toTrackAstroSubmitStatus(setFormState),\n    26→\t};\n    27→}\n    28→\n    29→export function useFormContext() {\n    30→\tconst formContext = useContext(FormContext);\n    31→\tif (!formContext) {\n    32→\t\tthrow new Error(\n    33→\t\t\t'Form context not found. `useFormContext()` should only be called from children of a <Form> component.'\n    34→\t\t);\n    35→\t}\n    36→\treturn formContext;\n    37→}\n    38→\n    39→type FormContextType = ReturnType<typeof useCreateFormContext>;\n    40→\n    41→const FormContext = createContext<FormContextType | undefined>(undefined);\n    42→\n    43→export function Form({\n    44→\tchildren,\n    45→\tvalidator,\n    46→\tcontext,\n    47→\tfieldErrors,\n    48→\tname,\n    49→\t...formProps\n    50→}: {\n    51→\tvalidator: FormValidator;\n    52→\tcontext?: FormContextType;\n    53→\tfieldErrors?: FieldErrors;\n    54→} & Omit<ComponentProps<'form'>, 'method' | 'onSubmit'>) {\n    55→\tconst formContext = context ?? useCreateFormContext(validator, fieldErrors);\n    56→\n    57→\treturn (\n    58→\t\t<FormContext.Provider value={formContext}>\n    59→\t\t\t<form\n    60→\t\t\t\t{...formProps}\n    61→\t\t\t\tmethod=\"POST\"\n    62→\t\t\t\tonSubmit={async (e) => {\n    63→\t\t\t\t\te.preventDefault();\n    64→\t\t\t\t\te.stopPropagation();\n    65→\t\t\t\t\tconst formData = new FormData(e.currentTarget);\n    66→\t\t\t\t\tformContext.set((formState) => ({\n    67→\t\t\t\t\t\t...formState,\n    68→\t\t\t\t\t\tisSubmitPending: true,\n    69→\t\t\t\t\t\tsubmitStatus: 'validating',\n    70→\t\t\t\t\t}));\n    71→\t\t\t\t\tconst parsed = await validateForm({ formData, validator });\n    72→\t\t\t\t\tif (parsed.data) {\n    73→\t\t\t\t\t\tnavigate(formProps.action ?? '', { formData });\n    74→\t\t\t\t\t\treturn formContext.trackAstroSubmitStatus();\n    75→\t\t\t\t\t}\n    76→\n    77→\t\t\t\t\tformContext.setValidationErrors(parsed.fieldErrors);\n    78→\t\t\t\t}}\n    79→\t\t\t>\n    80→\t\t\t\t{name ? <input {...formNameInputProps} value={name} /> : null}\n    81→\t\t\t\t{children}\n    82→\t\t\t</form>\n    83→\t\t</FormContext.Provider>\n    84→\t);\n    85→}\n    86→\n    87→export function Input(inputProps: ComponentProps<'input'> & { name: string }) {\n    88→\tconst formContext = useFormContext();\n    89→\tconst fieldState = formContext.value.fields[inputProps.name];\n    90→\tif (!fieldState) {\n    91→\t\tthrow new Error(\n    92→\t\t\t`Input \"${inputProps.name}\" not found in form. Did you use the <Form> component?`\n    93→\t\t);\n    94→\t}\n    95→\n    96→\tconst { hasErroredOnce, validationErrors, validator } = fieldState;\n    97→\treturn (\n    98→\t\t<>\n    99→\t\t\t<input\n   100→\t\t\t\tonBlur={async (e) => {\n   101→\t\t\t\t\tconst value = e.target.value;\n   102→\t\t\t\t\tif (value === '') return;\n   103→\t\t\t\t\tformContext.validateField(inputProps.name, value, validator);\n   104→\t\t\t\t}}\n   105→\t\t\t\tonChange={async (e) => {\n   106→\t\t\t\t\tif (!hasErroredOnce) return;\n   107→\t\t\t\t\tconst value = e.target.value;\n   108→\t\t\t\t\tformContext.validateField(inputProps.name, value, validator);\n   109→\t\t\t\t}}\n   110→\t\t\t\t{...inputProps}\n   111→\t\t\t/>\n   112→\t\t\t{validationErrors?.map((e) => (\n   113→\t\t\t\t<p className=\"error\" key={e}>\n   114→\t\t\t\t\t{e}\n   115→\t\t\t\t</p>\n   116→\t\t\t))}\n   117→\t\t</>\n   118→\t);\n   119→}\n   120→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01REm1BFVwZQZT3gEYb6usDZ","session_id":"ca373184-55de-43ea-b9dc-c45b48d70f8a","uuid":"407db1f8-fd57-4c1b-8950-8d0e8cca44b7"}
