{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011wVJPZ8cUqbQ4X8iTbfEmT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem: the `useEffect` for server updates has no dependency array, so it runs on every render. When it detects `prevFormRef.current !== form`, it updates state and calls `rerender()`, which causes another render, which runs the effect again. But on the second run, `prevFormRef.current === form` should be true so it should bail out... unless the `form` prop keeps a stable reference.\n\nWait, actually the test `mountForm` re-renders by passing a new `formProp` — but for the initial render, it shouldn't loop. Let me look more carefully. The issue might be that the test \"should handle cases when LiveView is not available\" renders without `LiveContext.Provider` and `useLive()` throws, but `try { useLive() } catch {}` should handle that...\n\nActually, I think the issue is subtler. The `useEffect` without deps runs after every render. When the component first mounts, `prevFormRef.current === form` is true (both set in the same render), so it returns early. That's fine. But when the test calls `rerender()` via `mountForm`, a new form object is passed, `prevFormRef.current !== form`, so it updates and calls `rerender()`, which triggers another render. On that render, `prevFormRef.current` was updated to `form` in the previous effect run, so `prevFormRef.current === form` → it returns early. So no infinite loop there.\n\nThe real problem might be something else. Let me try running just one simple test first."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_read_input_tokens":106985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca373184-55de-43ea-b9dc-c45b48d70f8a","uuid":