{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01W88QRKGsBfrg1i1jygdDN3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue is in the test. When rendering without `LiveContext.Provider`, `useLive()` throws, which is caught. But the `useEffect` for server updates still runs and tries to call `rerender()`. Actually wait — the problem is likely that when we render without a LiveContext, the `useEffect` with no dependency array runs after every render, but `prevFormRef.current === form` should be true on the first render since we set it in the same render pass...\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the test code:\n\n```js\nfunction TestComponent() {\n  capturedForm = useLiveForm(createFormData())  // Creates NEW form on each render!\n  return createElement(\"div\", null, \"test\")\n}\n```\n\nThe `createFormData()` is called on every render, creating a new object. So `prevFormRef.current !== form` is always true because the form object reference changes on every render. This causes `rerender()` to be called, which causes another render, infinite loop!\n\nThe fix is simple — in the test, create the form data outside the component."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":110640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca373184-55de-43ea-b9dc-c45b48d70f8a","uuid":"828de139-c8dc-440e-af38-9c53d749dbbb"}
