{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HXj2QF615cmpHTusrvkTN1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<promise>COMPLETE</promise>\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the React `useLiveForm` hook (`assets/useLiveFormReact.ts`) that mirrors the Vue `useLiveForm` composable for integrating with Ecto changesets and server-side form validation.\n\n### Files created:\n- **`assets/useLiveFormReact.ts`** — React hook implementation with:\n  - `useLiveForm(form, options)` — Main hook returning form state, field factories, submit/reset\n  - `useField(path, options)` — Child-component hook via `LiveFormContext`\n  - `useArrayField(path)` — Child-component array field hook via `LiveFormContext`\n  - `LiveFormContext` — React Context for form injection into children\n  - Full TypeScript interfaces: `ReactFormField<T>`, `ReactFormFieldArray<T>`, `UseLiveFormReactReturn<T>`\n\n- **`assets/useLiveFormReact.test.ts`** — 66 tests covering:\n  - Basic form initialization and deep cloning\n  - Field creation for simple, nested, and array paths\n  - Field value updates via `setValue()`\n  - Fluent sub-field creation interface\n  - Touched/dirty state tracking\n  - Form reset\n  - Validation errors from server\n  - `inputProps` helper (name, id, aria attributes, onChange, onBlur)\n  - Form-level dirty tracking\n  - Array field operations (add, remove, move, fields)\n  - LiveView integration (submit, debounced change events, server updates)\n  - Checkbox support (boolean, custom value, multi-checkbox)\n  - Field instance memoization\n\n### Files modified:\n- **`assets/index.ts`** — Added exports: `useLiveFormReact`, `useFieldReact`, `useArrayFieldReact`, `LiveFormContext`, and type exports\n\n### Key design decisions:\n- Uses a single mutable `store` ref pattern instead of `useCallback` dependencies to avoid stale closures and infinite re-render loops\n- Field objects use getter properties that read from the store on access, providing fresh values without React state overhead\n- A version counter (`useState`) triggers re-renders when mutable state changes\n- Server updates detected via `useEffect` comparing form object reference\n- Uses `onChange` (React convention) instead of Vue's `onInput` for `inputProps`\n- Re-uses `parsePath`, `getValueByPath`, `setValueByPath`, `sanitizeId` from shared utils"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":356,"cache_read_input_tokens":114816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":356},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca373184-55de-43ea-b9dc-c45b48d70f8a","uuid":"618ad766-076a-4b11-aed6-3b80c78e04fd"}
